1
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:44,090
This is so good!

2
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:45,670
Real good?

3
00:01:45,830 --> 00:01:50,490
The worst thing about the dungeon is not being able to eat this good when we're in it.

4
00:01:50,870 --> 00:01:52,530
Let's savor it while we can.

5
00:01:53,970 --> 00:01:55,410
Hey there, Kabru!

6
00:01:56,630 --> 00:01:58,090
Haven't seen you around.

7
00:01:58,090 --> 00:02:00,570
I heard you've been doing amazing lately.

8
00:02:01,050 --> 00:02:03,170
Well, I don't know about amazing.

9
00:02:03,710 --> 00:02:06,450
Seems like yesterday you all were just a bunch of rookies.

10
00:02:06,770 --> 00:02:07,730
But look at you now.

11
00:02:08,630 --> 00:02:10,530
It's great you guys are still together.

12
00:02:11,490 --> 00:02:13,570
Big parties are rare these days.

13
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:15,410
Why do you think that is?

14
00:02:15,910 --> 00:02:18,410
They go missing or just get sick of each other.

15
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:20,750
Fighting over money is a big reason.

16
00:02:21,290 --> 00:02:26,150
But your party's been together for a while, so maybe you'll be the ones to kill the Mad Mage.

17
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:27,910
Yeah, right.

18
00:02:28,370 --> 00:02:29,990
We're not that good yet.

19
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:31,310
Don't sell yourself short.

20
00:02:35,410 --> 00:02:36,750
Why are you like that?

21
00:02:37,230 --> 00:02:37,510
Huh?

22
00:02:38,150 --> 00:02:42,350
Instead of playing coy with that idiot, you should have just come right out and said it.

23
00:02:42,690 --> 00:02:45,450
Of course we'll be the ones to take out the Mad Mage.

24
00:02:45,830 --> 00:02:49,530
We could never settle for being bottom-rung adventurers such as that, Goon.

25
00:02:49,530 --> 00:02:57,870
Wren, Wren, they'll know us all by our actions instead of our words.

26
00:02:59,950 --> 00:03:00,870
Here's the plan.

27
00:03:01,190 --> 00:03:02,950
Today we'll go deeper into the dungeon.

28
00:03:03,630 --> 00:03:05,190
Let's gear up and get ready.

29
00:03:05,190 --> 00:03:16,330
Welcome.

30
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:18,030
Hello there.

31
00:03:18,470 --> 00:03:20,930
One week's food and two days' water for six people, please.

32
00:03:22,270 --> 00:03:23,230
Here you go.

33
00:03:23,230 --> 00:03:31,110
Dealing with food is a bigger pain than the monsters the deeper down we go.

34
00:03:31,530 --> 00:03:33,270
A week's worth of food is heavy.

35
00:03:34,050 --> 00:03:35,650
Some people stay in for a month.

36
00:03:35,850 --> 00:03:36,790
How do they do it?

37
00:03:37,510 --> 00:03:38,230
Well, McBell...

38
00:03:39,170 --> 00:03:42,230
What they do is...

39
00:03:42,230 --> 00:03:48,230
They kill the parties they meet and feast on their flesh!

40
00:03:48,230 --> 00:03:55,770
It'd be way easier to hunt monsters for food than other parties.

41
00:03:56,330 --> 00:03:58,590
You are what folks call a wet blanket.

42
00:04:06,730 --> 00:04:11,810
For our first time going down this deep, we're doing amazing.

43
00:04:12,630 --> 00:04:14,470
At this rate, we're going to get farther than anyone.

44
00:04:15,310 --> 00:04:17,750
Well, we're doing great so far, but stay sharp.

45
00:04:18,230 --> 00:04:20,050
Who knows what's waiting up ahead?

46
00:04:20,970 --> 00:04:23,370
I heard things have been strange here lately.

47
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:26,650
Some say the monsters are getting more aggressive.

48
00:04:27,330 --> 00:04:29,350
Others say the layout here has been changing.

49
00:04:30,010 --> 00:04:32,430
It definitely feels a lot weirder than before.

50
00:04:33,350 --> 00:04:34,930
Better to be safe than sorry.

51
00:04:35,210 --> 00:04:35,610
Kaurburu!

52
00:04:36,410 --> 00:04:37,290
Look at this!

53
00:04:37,630 --> 00:04:38,830
I got it off this zombie!

54
00:04:39,610 --> 00:04:40,390
Let's open it.

55
00:04:40,890 --> 00:04:42,870
Don't waste your time with that thing.

56
00:04:43,570 --> 00:04:44,690
What's the harm in checking?

57
00:04:45,030 --> 00:04:46,210
There could be gold in it.

58
00:04:46,210 --> 00:04:49,450
We've never found anything good in those before.

59
00:04:50,170 --> 00:04:54,690
There must be a good reason why this zombie had a death grip on it, literally speaking.

60
00:04:55,490 --> 00:04:57,350
It would be dumb to not take a peek.

61
00:04:58,250 --> 00:04:58,550
Huh?

62
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:00,090
No way!

63
00:05:00,810 --> 00:05:01,870
Gold and jewels!

64
00:05:02,370 --> 00:05:03,570
We hit the jackpot!

65
00:05:03,570 --> 00:05:06,470
We're rich!

66
00:05:06,730 --> 00:05:07,950
I can't believe it!

67
00:05:08,030 --> 00:05:08,590
Hot diggity.

68
00:05:08,870 --> 00:05:09,570
What a hole.

69
00:05:11,810 --> 00:05:15,290
I thought by now the dungeon would be picked clean of all the treasure.

70
00:05:16,230 --> 00:05:16,690
Oh well.

71
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:19,170
Like they say, things happen strange here.

72
00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:27,150
We so needed a brick like this.

73
00:05:27,630 --> 00:05:30,110
Now we can afford the supplies we need to go deeper.

74
00:05:31,590 --> 00:05:34,430
Guys, how about we all head back to town for some dinner?

75
00:05:34,930 --> 00:05:35,610
Does that sound good?

76
00:05:35,610 --> 00:05:36,570
Yeah!

77
00:05:36,570 --> 00:05:36,850
Yeah!

78
00:05:43,850 --> 00:05:44,370
Huh?

79
00:05:45,210 --> 00:05:45,730
Whoa.

80
00:05:46,570 --> 00:05:48,750
These guys got wiped out big time.

81
00:05:48,930 --> 00:05:49,510
Oh no.

82
00:05:49,830 --> 00:05:51,990
Looks like they were headed back to town too.

83
00:05:52,530 --> 00:05:53,390
How awful.

84
00:05:54,030 --> 00:05:55,850
I don't see any wounds on them.

85
00:05:56,350 --> 00:05:57,470
Maybe a ghost killed them.

86
00:05:58,330 --> 00:05:59,950
Or they starved to death.

87
00:06:00,410 --> 00:06:03,330
And it looks to me like they killed each other over this treasure.

88
00:06:03,330 --> 00:06:08,850
I, um, I'm sure the corpse retrievers will find them soon.

89
00:06:09,270 --> 00:06:11,810
But I'll cast a spell so they don't turn into zombies.

90
00:06:12,590 --> 00:06:14,610
This was Fallon's specialty though.

91
00:06:19,490 --> 00:06:21,570
What do you want to do about all this treasure?

92
00:06:22,250 --> 00:06:24,110
Let's pile it up and leave it for them.

93
00:06:24,650 --> 00:06:28,130
I bet most of it's gonna end up in the pockets of the corpse retrievers.

94
00:06:30,450 --> 00:06:30,850
What?

95
00:06:31,150 --> 00:06:32,310
Are you okay back there?

96
00:06:32,550 --> 00:06:32,890
Yeah.

97
00:06:33,330 --> 00:06:33,850
Sure am.

98
00:06:35,130 --> 00:06:36,590
Why'd my sword twitch?

99
00:06:39,370 --> 00:06:41,090
Hey, let go of my hand.

100
00:06:41,670 --> 00:06:43,030
You're gonna give yourself away.

101
00:06:43,330 --> 00:06:44,150
What do you want?

102
00:06:46,950 --> 00:06:47,510
Hurry.

103
00:06:48,050 --> 00:06:48,870
Draw me.

104
00:06:49,470 --> 00:06:51,790
I can feel it telling me there's danger.

105
00:06:51,790 --> 00:06:52,130
Marcel!

106
00:06:57,610 --> 00:06:58,010
Ah!

107
00:07:02,590 --> 00:07:02,990
Marcel!

108
00:07:03,350 --> 00:07:04,230
Get away from there!

109
00:07:04,450 --> 00:07:04,610
Ah!

110
00:07:04,610 --> 00:07:05,610
Huh?

111
00:07:09,610 --> 00:07:10,610
Huh?

112
00:07:29,610 --> 00:07:31,610
A stun spell.

113
00:07:31,610 --> 00:07:35,610
I'm glad it wasn't an explosion spell.

114
00:07:35,610 --> 00:07:38,610
What the heck? Treasure insects?

115
00:07:38,610 --> 00:07:39,610
Oh, gross!

116
00:07:41,610 --> 00:07:45,610
Bees killed them? Never seen one up close like this before.

117
00:07:45,610 --> 00:07:48,610
I can't tell the difference from real treasure.

118
00:07:48,610 --> 00:07:50,610
But a minute ago you could tell.

119
00:07:50,610 --> 00:07:53,610
Yeah, he's right. You even drew your sword.

120
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:57,610
Oh, um, I thought I saw one of them move?

121
00:07:57,610 --> 00:07:58,610
Liar.

122
00:07:58,610 --> 00:08:01,610
The critter and my sword sensed them.

123
00:08:01,610 --> 00:08:04,610
It's calm now, so that's gotta be it.

124
00:08:06,610 --> 00:08:09,610
Is it just me or is it getting weirder?

125
00:08:09,610 --> 00:08:10,610
Huh?

126
00:08:10,610 --> 00:08:11,610
Hmm.

127
00:08:11,610 --> 00:08:12,610
Yum.

128
00:08:12,610 --> 00:08:15,610
You have got to be kidding me.

129
00:08:15,610 --> 00:08:16,610
You have got to be kidding me.

130
00:08:16,610 --> 00:08:30,610
These you can eat. These you can't.

131
00:08:30,610 --> 00:08:32,610
Do they taste any good?

132
00:08:32,610 --> 00:08:34,610
Oh, I'll say they do.

133
00:08:34,610 --> 00:08:36,610
Bugs got all the nutrients a body needs.

134
00:08:36,610 --> 00:08:39,610
Cook these suckers up right and you got yourself a meal.

135
00:08:39,610 --> 00:08:42,610
Hell, they're a feast for the eyes, too.

136
00:08:42,610 --> 00:08:44,610
Not if you're seeing it from this angle.

137
00:08:44,610 --> 00:08:47,610
How can you tell which are or aren't edible?

138
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,610
Hmm, it depends.

139
00:08:49,610 --> 00:08:51,610
For example, this one's easy.

140
00:08:51,610 --> 00:08:56,610
If you look between the beads, you can see its teeny legs.

141
00:08:56,610 --> 00:08:59,610
With brooches and coins, you check the backside.

142
00:08:59,610 --> 00:09:03,610
I think it's neat how the male and female coin bugs have different faces.

143
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:06,610
With rings, if they're flexible, they're a bug.

144
00:09:06,610 --> 00:09:10,610
Tiaras need to be put in water to tell for sure.

145
00:09:10,610 --> 00:09:15,610
Bugs are light, so if it floats, you got yourself bugs.

146
00:09:15,610 --> 00:09:19,610
Let's cook these suckers before the stun spell wears off.

147
00:09:19,610 --> 00:09:22,610
For the necklace, pull off all the legs.

148
00:09:22,610 --> 00:09:25,610
The texture ain't great if you leave them on.

149
00:09:25,610 --> 00:09:27,610
Then skewer and roast it.

150
00:09:27,610 --> 00:09:32,610
Heat up some oil and give the coin bugs a good frown, stomach side down.

151
00:09:32,610 --> 00:09:37,610
Drop in a pinch of salt and stir them so the oil gets around evenly.

152
00:09:37,610 --> 00:09:39,610
There.

153
00:09:39,610 --> 00:09:42,610
Flip them spine side up so they look pretty.

154
00:09:42,610 --> 00:09:46,610
Pour the tiara, pop out the eggs and larva from their nest.

155
00:09:46,610 --> 00:09:49,610
Risk it up in the pot and boil everything together.

156
00:09:51,610 --> 00:09:54,610
Spoon it into a jar and...

157
00:09:54,610 --> 00:09:56,610
It's ready.

158
00:09:56,610 --> 00:10:03,610
Looks nice, but they still don't look much like food to me.

159
00:10:03,610 --> 00:10:07,610
Then again, it's not my first time eating these things.

160
00:10:07,610 --> 00:10:09,610
I heard they're some kind of regional cuisine.

161
00:10:09,610 --> 00:10:11,610
Some say eating them brings luck.

162
00:10:11,610 --> 00:10:13,610
I'll find out in a sec.

163
00:10:15,610 --> 00:10:18,610
Those taste way better than the ones I had.

164
00:10:18,610 --> 00:10:20,610
Of course it does.

165
00:10:20,610 --> 00:10:24,610
The monsters you get from the dungeon always got better flavor than the ones on the surface.

166
00:10:24,610 --> 00:10:29,610
Folks up top can try raising them, but they just don't taste the same.

167
00:10:29,610 --> 00:10:30,610
Uh...

168
00:10:30,610 --> 00:10:31,610
Uh...

169
00:10:31,610 --> 00:10:32,610
Uh...

170
00:10:32,610 --> 00:10:33,610
Uh...

171
00:10:33,610 --> 00:10:34,610
Uh...

172
00:10:34,610 --> 00:10:35,610
Uh...

173
00:10:35,610 --> 00:10:36,610
Uh...

174
00:10:36,610 --> 00:10:37,610
Uh...

175
00:10:37,610 --> 00:10:38,610
Uh...

176
00:10:38,610 --> 00:10:39,610
Uh...

177
00:10:39,610 --> 00:10:41,610
Dear lord, it's creamy.

178
00:10:41,610 --> 00:10:44,610
I'm never gonna wear neckses again.

179
00:10:44,610 --> 00:10:46,610
This kinda tastes like fish.

180
00:10:46,610 --> 00:10:47,610
Ow!

181
00:10:47,610 --> 00:10:50,610
If we find some deeper down, they'll taste even better.

182
00:10:50,610 --> 00:10:51,610
I can't wait.

183
00:10:51,610 --> 00:10:52,610
Oh!

184
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:53,610
Thank you.

185
00:10:53,610 --> 00:10:54,610
Ow!

186
00:10:54,610 --> 00:10:55,610
Mm.

187
00:10:55,610 --> 00:10:56,610
Mm.

188
00:10:56,610 --> 00:10:57,610
Mm.

189
00:10:57,610 --> 00:10:58,610
Wow.

190
00:10:58,610 --> 00:10:59,610
That's sweet.

191
00:10:59,610 --> 00:11:02,610
Can't get over how real they look.

192
00:11:02,610 --> 00:11:05,610
They use mimicry to hide from their enemies.

193
00:11:05,610 --> 00:11:07,610
Just like you, sword critter.

194
00:11:07,610 --> 00:11:10,610
Is that why you reacted to them?

195
00:11:10,610 --> 00:11:11,610
Hmm.

196
00:11:11,610 --> 00:11:12,610
Mm.

197
00:11:12,610 --> 00:11:13,610
Mm.

198
00:11:13,610 --> 00:11:14,610
Can I try one?

199
00:11:14,610 --> 00:11:15,610
Hm.

200
00:11:15,610 --> 00:11:16,610
Hmm.

201
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:17,610
Hmm.

202
00:11:17,610 --> 00:11:18,610
Hmm.

203
00:11:18,610 --> 00:11:19,610
Huh?

204
00:11:19,610 --> 00:11:20,610
Huh?

205
00:11:20,610 --> 00:11:21,610
Huh?

206
00:11:21,610 --> 00:11:22,610
It's nothing.

207
00:11:22,610 --> 00:11:23,610
Oh.

208
00:11:23,610 --> 00:11:24,610
It thought it was a threat.

209
00:11:24,610 --> 00:11:25,610
It was trying to warn me.

210
00:11:25,610 --> 00:11:26,610
I think it thinks we're a team now.

211
00:11:26,610 --> 00:11:27,610
How cute.

212
00:11:27,610 --> 00:11:28,610
I have to give you a name.

213
00:11:28,610 --> 00:11:29,610
Ready to get going?

214
00:11:29,610 --> 00:11:32,610
What are we supposed to do with the ones you said we can't eat?

215
00:11:32,610 --> 00:11:33,610
Toss them, if you want.

216
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:34,610
If someone were to eat one of these, what would you do?

217
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:35,610
What would you do?

218
00:11:35,610 --> 00:11:36,610
What would you do with the ones you said we can't eat?

219
00:11:36,610 --> 00:11:38,610
Toss them, if you want.

220
00:11:38,610 --> 00:11:39,610
If someone were to eat one of these, what would you do?

221
00:11:39,610 --> 00:11:40,610
What would you do with them?

222
00:11:40,610 --> 00:11:42,610
Are they poisonous or do they just taste bad?

223
00:11:42,610 --> 00:11:43,610
What are you talking about?

224
00:11:43,610 --> 00:11:44,610
You'd break your teeth.

225
00:11:44,610 --> 00:11:45,610
You can't eat real treasure.

226
00:11:45,610 --> 00:11:46,610
You could break your teeth.

227
00:11:46,610 --> 00:11:47,610
You can't eat real treasure.

228
00:11:47,610 --> 00:11:48,610
What would you do with me?

229
00:11:48,610 --> 00:11:49,610
What would you do with them now?

230
00:11:49,610 --> 00:11:50,610
How cute.

231
00:11:50,610 --> 00:11:51,610
I have to give you a name?

232
00:11:51,610 --> 00:11:52,610
Ready to get going?

233
00:11:52,610 --> 00:11:53,610
What are we supposed to do with the ones you said we can't eat?

234
00:11:53,610 --> 00:11:54,610
Toss them, if you want.

235
00:11:54,610 --> 00:11:55,610
If someone were to eat one of these, what would happen to them?

236
00:11:55,610 --> 00:11:56,610
Don't you tell them, not to their own house?

237
00:11:56,610 --> 00:11:57,610
You need to drink.

238
00:11:57,610 --> 00:11:58,610
What are you talking about?

239
00:11:58,610 --> 00:12:00,610
You break your teeth.

240
00:12:00,610 --> 00:12:05,610
You can't eat real treasure.

241
00:12:05,610 --> 00:12:08,610
You break your teeth.

242
00:12:08,610 --> 00:12:10,730
Real treasure. Real treasure.

243
00:12:11,610 --> 00:12:13,190
Treasure. Treasure.

244
00:12:13,850 --> 00:12:16,310
Why didn't you say that before?

245
00:12:19,730 --> 00:12:20,610
Got it.

246
00:12:20,830 --> 00:12:22,630
From now on, your name's Kensuke.

247
00:12:35,110 --> 00:12:37,350
You're eating another one of those things?

248
00:12:37,350 --> 00:12:38,870
We got a lot of leftovers.

249
00:12:39,490 --> 00:12:41,570
Honestly, this isn't a picnic.

250
00:12:47,710 --> 00:12:49,530
Great. The temperature dropped.

251
00:12:51,130 --> 00:12:53,410
All those shimmery blobs.

252
00:12:54,630 --> 00:12:56,370
Yeah, those are ghosts gathering.

253
00:12:56,970 --> 00:12:58,670
Go, before they see us.

254
00:13:00,030 --> 00:13:00,710
Ghosts?

255
00:13:01,190 --> 00:13:03,650
They're drawn to the corpses we just left behind.

256
00:13:03,650 --> 00:13:07,650
Hmm. We should just blast them with a spell and...

257
00:13:08,450 --> 00:13:10,610
That's right.

258
00:13:11,250 --> 00:13:12,330
Fallon's not here.

259
00:13:13,230 --> 00:13:14,130
I miss her, too.

260
00:13:15,170 --> 00:13:17,470
I cast a protection spell on that party.

261
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:20,650
I had to rush it a bit, but the ghosts won't possess...

262
00:13:21,350 --> 00:13:28,610
Ghost. Behind us. Run!

263
00:13:28,610 --> 00:13:47,130
Oh, that idiot!

264
00:13:47,130 --> 00:13:57,930
My ears.

265
00:13:57,930 --> 00:13:59,790
Hurry, get up. More are coming.

266
00:14:02,790 --> 00:14:04,970
They're all riled up from that explosion.

267
00:14:04,970 --> 00:14:10,670
Don't you know any less flashy magic spells?

268
00:14:11,090 --> 00:14:12,530
You know, something simple?

269
00:14:12,690 --> 00:14:14,290
Like the kind Fallon always used.

270
00:14:14,570 --> 00:14:15,670
Are you kidding me?

271
00:14:15,810 --> 00:14:17,270
She used high-level magic.

272
00:14:17,470 --> 00:14:19,210
There was nothing simple about it.

273
00:14:19,290 --> 00:14:19,590
Really?

274
00:14:19,930 --> 00:14:20,470
Oh, yeah.

275
00:14:21,050 --> 00:14:21,710
It's true.

276
00:14:22,350 --> 00:14:23,790
She's an awesome magic user.

277
00:14:24,710 --> 00:14:26,910
Dealing with ghosts was no sweat for her.

278
00:14:26,910 --> 00:14:28,570
Lifgant.

279
00:14:29,450 --> 00:14:30,090
Odenbaum.

280
00:14:31,990 --> 00:14:32,550
There!

281
00:14:33,150 --> 00:14:34,430
That's all there is to it.

282
00:14:35,030 --> 00:14:37,050
Those pesky ghosts can't harm you now.

283
00:14:38,710 --> 00:14:42,750
If any show up, an explosion spell could take them all out quick.

284
00:14:43,270 --> 00:14:44,670
You could do that easy, Fallon.

285
00:14:47,290 --> 00:14:50,290
If possible, I'd prefer to avoid doing that.

286
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:52,370
It doesn't get rid of them.

287
00:14:52,810 --> 00:14:55,630
After they're blown to bits, they just reform again anyway.

288
00:14:56,170 --> 00:14:57,790
And I don't want to make them suffer.

289
00:14:58,470 --> 00:14:59,790
You're so kind.

290
00:14:59,970 --> 00:15:02,310
That's nice you're giving them the benefit of the doubt.

291
00:15:03,870 --> 00:15:06,370
But if ghosts go around possessing people's bodies...

292
00:15:07,110 --> 00:15:10,730
I think they deserve to get their butts kicked.

293
00:15:16,590 --> 00:15:17,230
Mm-hmm.

294
00:15:17,770 --> 00:15:20,330
That guy's on the missing adventurer list, all right.

295
00:15:20,330 --> 00:15:23,670
Okay, I'll take care of them.

296
00:15:24,230 --> 00:15:25,810
First, I'll knock them...

297
00:15:25,810 --> 00:15:27,610
I'll do it.

298
00:15:27,990 --> 00:15:30,130
This can be handled without violence.

299
00:15:31,830 --> 00:15:32,310
No!

300
00:15:32,670 --> 00:15:33,410
Fallon, wait!

301
00:15:45,410 --> 00:15:46,530
Be at peace.

302
00:15:47,230 --> 00:15:48,290
And leave this body.

303
00:15:50,330 --> 00:15:55,030
Fallon!

304
00:16:01,830 --> 00:16:03,850
She sounds like a heck of a person.

305
00:16:04,590 --> 00:16:05,030
Yeah.

306
00:16:05,470 --> 00:16:06,770
Fallon was amazing.

307
00:16:07,090 --> 00:16:07,890
I mean, is.

308
00:16:08,870 --> 00:16:09,710
But...

309
00:16:09,710 --> 00:16:12,330
If the ghosts catch up to us...

310
00:16:12,330 --> 00:16:15,250
I'll have to use my magic to stop them.

311
00:16:15,250 --> 00:16:16,570
Oh, no, you won't.

312
00:16:16,790 --> 00:16:19,330
There's no way you can blow up every single one of them.

313
00:16:23,390 --> 00:16:25,370
I'll do it just like Fallon did.

314
00:16:26,030 --> 00:16:28,430
I'll give them all a gentle embrace.

315
00:16:28,890 --> 00:16:30,930
A gentle embrace of explosions.

316
00:16:31,170 --> 00:16:31,430
No.

317
00:16:31,590 --> 00:16:32,070
Gentle explosions.

318
00:16:32,070 --> 00:16:32,230
No!

319
00:16:32,710 --> 00:16:33,090
No!

320
00:16:33,490 --> 00:16:36,770
You said yourself you can't do it like Fallon, so just leave them alone!

321
00:16:36,910 --> 00:16:38,590
She'd trust me to do the right thing!

322
00:16:39,050 --> 00:16:41,230
Okay, then what will you do if you run out of mana?

323
00:16:41,430 --> 00:16:42,110
I won't.

324
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:45,050
I can use my weaker explosion spells to blow them up.

325
00:16:45,250 --> 00:16:47,290
There are no weak explosion spells!

326
00:16:47,450 --> 00:16:48,510
Guys, enough.

327
00:16:48,930 --> 00:16:52,310
Hate to say it, folks, but it don't look like we're gonna outrun these creepies.

328
00:16:53,410 --> 00:16:57,730
The longer we stand around arguing, the faster they'll catch up to us.

329
00:16:59,050 --> 00:17:01,070
Wait, what are you doing?

330
00:17:01,470 --> 00:17:04,170
Gonna whip up a little something to keep the ghosts off us.

331
00:17:04,970 --> 00:17:06,130
What kind of thing?

332
00:17:06,330 --> 00:17:07,530
A holy water thing.

333
00:17:07,730 --> 00:17:08,950
Wait, you have holy water?

334
00:17:09,490 --> 00:17:09,750
Nope.

335
00:17:10,270 --> 00:17:11,070
Gotta make some.

336
00:17:11,770 --> 00:17:13,330
You can make that?

337
00:17:13,710 --> 00:17:15,250
Didn't know you were a cleric, too.

338
00:17:17,170 --> 00:17:20,350
There's all kinds of custom in the world to get rid of evil stuff.

339
00:17:21,690 --> 00:17:22,710
Fire's one of them.

340
00:17:23,190 --> 00:17:25,970
It keeps the dark back, and it can create and destroy.

341
00:17:26,550 --> 00:17:32,490
All through history, folks have used it as a sacred symbol and a holy ward to keep that evil the hell away from you.

342
00:17:32,490 --> 00:17:37,010
Yeah, I know all that, but candles aren't gonna keep ghosts back.

343
00:17:37,330 --> 00:17:41,350
One candle might not help much, but a bunch of them all lit up and flickering away?

344
00:17:41,770 --> 00:17:43,050
That's a lot of holy power.

345
00:17:43,690 --> 00:17:46,310
The golden rhinoceros beetle's another secret thing.

346
00:17:46,710 --> 00:17:50,010
To some folks, they were symbols of the sun and the sun god.

347
00:17:50,590 --> 00:17:52,150
A lot of love for those critters.

348
00:17:53,250 --> 00:17:54,350
Ooze is holy, too.

349
00:17:54,350 --> 00:17:58,810
It's used as an offering to the gods and to purify whatever it is it needs purifying.

350
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:01,410
Then there's salt.

351
00:18:01,770 --> 00:18:05,990
Tradition's going way back, saying it protects against evil and purifies the body.

352
00:18:06,750 --> 00:18:09,170
And since sugar looks the same, I'll add some of that.

353
00:18:09,610 --> 00:18:12,810
Not sure how potent it'll be, so I'll dump a bunch in to be safe.

354
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:14,510
You're making this up as you go!

355
00:18:15,190 --> 00:18:16,830
Not a bad idea to add some herbs.

356
00:18:17,190 --> 00:18:19,390
And what the heck, dried monster guts, too.

357
00:18:19,390 --> 00:18:22,150
Then we'll add the power of fire to the mix.

358
00:18:25,190 --> 00:18:26,850
The holy water's ready.

359
00:18:31,070 --> 00:18:32,050
Here they come!

360
00:18:32,470 --> 00:18:35,090
Just gotta make sure the lid's tight on the holy water.

361
00:18:35,490 --> 00:18:37,490
What are you doing? Aren't you gonna use it?

362
00:18:37,610 --> 00:18:40,310
I will, as soon as I tie this rope to the jar.

363
00:18:43,130 --> 00:18:44,810
We're gonna die here.

364
00:18:49,390 --> 00:18:54,590
Oh, no.

365
00:18:56,730 --> 00:18:57,290
Thelen.

366
00:19:01,630 --> 00:19:02,810
I'm alive.

367
00:19:03,530 --> 00:19:04,310
Because of you.

368
00:19:05,670 --> 00:19:08,270
If only the dragon ate me instead,

369
00:19:09,190 --> 00:19:11,030
our friends wouldn't be in this mess.

370
00:19:13,630 --> 00:19:14,550
Forgive me.

371
00:19:14,550 --> 00:19:39,030
Holy crap!

372
00:19:39,330 --> 00:19:40,970
I saw my dad on the other side!

373
00:19:42,970 --> 00:19:44,210
It's working.

374
00:19:44,870 --> 00:19:47,370
Every ghost he hits gets driven away.

375
00:19:53,130 --> 00:19:54,470
Only water works.

376
00:19:54,790 --> 00:19:55,710
Even in a jar.

377
00:19:55,930 --> 00:19:57,170
It works amazingly.

378
00:20:00,450 --> 00:20:04,070
Maybe I've been possessed this whole time by Fallon.

379
00:20:04,610 --> 00:20:06,130
How could you say that?

380
00:20:06,370 --> 00:20:07,330
Fallon would never.

381
00:20:07,730 --> 00:20:09,870
And she hasn't even turned into a ghost yet.

382
00:20:10,150 --> 00:20:11,450
No, that's not what I mean.

383
00:20:11,450 --> 00:20:15,430
I couldn't get over the fact that we don't have her help.

384
00:20:15,810 --> 00:20:18,330
And thinking about how easy things would be if we did.

385
00:20:18,970 --> 00:20:21,050
But the reality is, she's not here.

386
00:20:22,330 --> 00:20:24,710
Until she's back, we gotta help ourselves.

387
00:20:24,710 --> 00:20:29,750
Yeah, you're right.

388
00:20:31,370 --> 00:20:31,870
Senchi!

389
00:20:31,870 --> 00:20:34,290
Let me take a crack at him.

390
00:20:34,290 --> 00:20:42,950
It's over.

391
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:51,950
It's over.

392
00:20:51,950 --> 00:20:56,790
The jar's got frost on it.

393
00:20:58,190 --> 00:21:01,850
Using holy water like that's more efficient than spraying it all over.

394
00:21:02,330 --> 00:21:03,150
That figures.

395
00:21:03,570 --> 00:21:06,010
Ghost can pass through the jar so the water hits him.

396
00:21:06,490 --> 00:21:06,730
Hmm?

397
00:21:07,790 --> 00:21:09,110
Well, I'll be.

398
00:21:09,110 --> 00:21:16,390
It's sorbet.

399
00:21:21,890 --> 00:21:25,330
Is it safe to eat something with ghost funk all over it?

400
00:21:25,810 --> 00:21:30,550
I'm more worried about what holy water this powerful is gonna do to our stomachs.

401
00:21:30,770 --> 00:21:33,270
I'm worried about how much sugar I've had today.

402
00:21:33,270 --> 00:21:39,470
It's great!

403
00:21:46,270 --> 00:21:47,190
He's right!

404
00:21:47,530 --> 00:21:48,130
It's good!

405
00:21:48,490 --> 00:21:50,470
It's so light and refreshing, too!

406
00:21:52,410 --> 00:21:55,090
Instead of getting cursed by ghosts, we got blessed.

407
00:21:55,490 --> 00:21:56,330
You said it!

408
00:21:56,330 --> 00:21:58,410
You said there's monster in this.

409
00:21:58,630 --> 00:21:59,490
What did you end up using?

410
00:22:00,090 --> 00:22:01,590
Just some grated slime guts.

411
00:22:02,290 --> 00:22:04,410
Oh, that explains the jiggly texture.

412
00:22:04,770 --> 00:22:06,830
But it's still so smooth and creamy.

413
00:22:09,830 --> 00:22:10,870
Hey, guys.

414
00:22:11,770 --> 00:22:12,870
Get this.

415
00:22:14,170 --> 00:22:15,550
We're so lucky.

416
00:22:15,910 --> 00:22:18,830
If Fallon didn't get eaten, we wouldn't be having sorbet now.

417
00:22:20,470 --> 00:22:21,110
Huh?

418
00:22:22,110 --> 00:22:23,590
You're joking, right?

419
00:22:23,590 --> 00:22:26,670
It sounds like you're happy that she got eaten.

420
00:22:26,790 --> 00:22:29,070
You're, like, the worst brother ever!

421
00:22:29,370 --> 00:22:31,990
But I was just saying...

422
00:22:31,990 --> 00:22:34,910
You know, some things are better to keep to yourself.

423
00:22:36,730 --> 00:22:41,290
Oh, jeez.

424
00:22:41,550 --> 00:22:42,930
If only Fallon were here.

425
00:22:44,330 --> 00:22:47,130
There's a positive side to every bad situation.

426
00:22:47,610 --> 00:22:50,090
She'd say something like that and pack me up.

427
00:22:51,030 --> 00:22:53,770
I don't know if it's me or this sorbet,

428
00:22:53,990 --> 00:22:55,790
but the vibe here got chillier.

429
00:22:56,490 --> 00:22:57,810
Come back, Fallon.

430
00:22:57,950 --> 00:22:58,950
We need you!

